{"title":"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Side_note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Side note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(No_Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (No Trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has positive integer side lengths with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of the bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4056d41f42aa8a00adca0ff5d1209b6bb0e92d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef7345911077c0f466f96fa1dd13b774afeba54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. Find the smallest possible perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Side_note\">Side note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Side note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This problem also made a debut in the recent 2026 AIME II, specifically P8. Check that out as well!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Then by SAS Congruence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6ced03b65392658a852f181761498f6e964fc7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/5658074c7dc8e0146df8a45bdcbfbf0d762e6152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB = \\angle ADC = 90^o$\" width=\"186\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d8553582f0b6fb27e92102a8ba39b074975ab770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598141cec89bb44405e53c44ba75a25f8b5981bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cfaf1e419e96239839bd5517604eda87ba92b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IBD = \\dfrac{\\angle ABD}{2} = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a509f77f7a1f55643fd9c2c1bdccfd2c3b524d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{cos}{(\\theta)} = \\dfrac{y}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d056deaf3c27e20880c89e5fe05d6a1f72ab7f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{cos}{(2\\theta)} = \\dfrac{y}{x} = 2\\mathrm{cos^2}{(\\theta)} - 1 = \\dfrac{y^2-32}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"298\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Cross-multiplying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc102d944d9993853355a513d0501e0e62b34b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32y = x(y^2-32)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c2cebdbc524624cf9bab853640b2d6e8b00320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acb8b027c491b996fcf8c1edc471dc3e747d70b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> must be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73eb2e6c5e511ebaea2f646260ccabee698c3aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; 5.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Additionally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f70d3b15c99045fe09e41004ec9befbcc089fae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle IBD$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> has hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947f44aa6d262217b9db497fef4b9ef25833beb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{IB}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9675cbd4c79687547f2d43c2c0d8f23ea81bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=y &lt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c91a53e7d0b72f7d6d8b19cdd6b62461a3ff34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer, the only possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7314f8133d3b925b9ce6598191d153da7ecdd779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/0548d22c8d43aa7314709ed34e7c106d4057beb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>However, only one of these values, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daaf07d9f0a2413768e291d1264b59b3c835e4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, yields an integral value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598141cec89bb44405e53c44ba75a25f8b5981bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, so we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daaf07d9f0a2413768e291d1264b59b3c835e4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba24cd243315a49fb0da9f0520d6d8ca2904797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{32(6)}{(6)^2-32}=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"151\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7d7129c6a9870408c19160335e804e2f363a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(x+y) = \\boxed{108}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"130\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28No_Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(No_Trig)\">Solution 2 (No Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (No Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598141cec89bb44405e53c44ba75a25f8b5981bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c8600ab2461faa433aeeda9dd145cf257d94ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. Since ABC is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. By Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566310379fe435fe0bee52fa7f45066fda98b532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\sqrt{x^2-y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"22\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07d9246071ad4d82279bfe516ec5a534496ff1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IE=a$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1daa65decf96a9fb091e5312dc7cec4af7819a0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IA=b$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />. By Angle Bisector theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53894573aa814c4e8058c2871ad463e2236b7317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{a}=\\frac{x}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcdc6522a8224276e912429650245a0a780099f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\sqrt{x^2-y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"22\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2eb8861befe3186ccbed4d8bb2aab994345470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2-y^2}}{1+\\frac{x}{y}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"108\" height=\"47\" />. Then, using Pythagorean Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/8829ec859901d9365248d6c4f3a8284d0ac595c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEI$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b5077332ce8d4a54a863537c8ac47f09745305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2-y^2}}{1+\\frac{x}{y}}\\right)^2=8^2=64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"234\" height=\"56\" />. Simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/298243cf818fa54806d1e9ca8f8cf058c0d533ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2+y^2\\frac{x^2-y^2}{(x+y)^2}=64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"166\" height=\"43\" />. Factoring out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd7a3b5db37d02e7cef42adc65c389a0047647e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2\\left(1+\\frac{x^2-y^2}{(x+y)^2}\\right)=64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"187\" height=\"43\" />. Adding 1 to the fraction and simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9ae0d67612e26fe4ec9632cd40964f3de6d7cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y^2x(x+y)}{(x+y)^2}=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"129\" height=\"43\" />. Crossing out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc102d944d9993853355a513d0501e0e62b34b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32y = x(y^2-32)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" />. Then, we continue as Solution 1 does.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598141cec89bb44405e53c44ba75a25f8b5981bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, call the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, call the point where the incircle meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, \n</p><p>and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c8600ab2461faa433aeeda9dd145cf257d94ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. We are looking for the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c3184c8f254384d4b2ed88a6512dd7ee91612f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is an altitude because the triangle\n</p><p>is isosceles. By Pythagoras on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d9089da1502dec8c26b0296812dc691ea5f313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEI$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" />, the inradius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de93bed7134fc10638e02b1cf5d3a56cab5dcbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{64-y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"22\" /> and by Pythagoras on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/534a193c938ab7c56417c466dd06d87736aa3084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2-y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"22\" />. By equal tangents, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e394df3494109d3bf50fd4175a78a71bb469356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=BD=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8cb7d67dc6524996eb96c3ac86ce11a33c11597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0bfbf26e6ab98a461a5cb0964c6778a20122f07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ID$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> is an inradius, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217dbc4aa69d3c1dcf703132de964061930b10b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ID=IE$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" /> and\nusing pythagoras on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b7cb3327556065c4092ed18c2ad82a53a07f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADI$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51ed2a38ea6a6c543cdc08b1702805ce65f60e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI=$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc93fc99eb7f8114a29634c1b7a41b9a48fb0708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2-2xy+64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"22\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b7cb3327556065c4092ed18c2ad82a53a07f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADI$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ece55f9a0c8c69d74514764c04b2a52b1cf734e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b3dbb5e0c16cabfa02f10ace626714ac385dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, so we \n</p><p>can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e961d0032bb14d0c0faeb970b50e846a73e51a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x-y}{\\sqrt{x^2-2xy+64}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2-y^2}}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"227\" height=\"44\" />. Simplifying, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a58484df473b88b00faad9e850e019ce309a14a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2-2xy+64}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+y}{x-y}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"217\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Squaring, subtracting 1 from both sides, and multiplying everything out, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1aff2ed8b25b0d30ca933f9e91813c8d5dbc6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yx^2-2xy^2+64y=yx^2 -32x+32y-xy^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"336\" height=\"18\" />, which turns into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc5ffdcf0937ffbfc7dfd3a3cad7a4507eaa0da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32y=x(y^2-32)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" />. Finish as in Solution 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Angle bisectors motivate trig bash. \nDefine angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf56f0b220d0630d0c392a1cacf35b1a8cde790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IBC = x$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />. Foot of perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d6aafa7a5d25c31309e1285d7c0365f8e6a02c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC} = 2\\overline{BP} = 2(8\\cos(x)) = N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc51e20be2982ee3e8c2f41070e57fe24d1edb5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x) = \\frac{N}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />. Via double angle, we calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/818c09f3a8aae8dd78b4975e153d23f7474958d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8\\cos(x)}{2\\cos(x)^2 - 1} = \\frac{64N}{N^2 - 128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"204\" height=\"43\" />. This is to be an integer.  We can bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> now, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef87d638a6889dbae475d0f2b8b29697b39f7762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N &gt; 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> to avoid negative values and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9f34b5a01b67b1d58e5f0c9ec870427dd4bb7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N &lt; 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> due to triangle inequality. Testing, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a2b1091166a6e32e6ddaec65386d3e713011cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> works, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7de58f3aff4d71e4f10a6a27448762c4d53c1d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} = 48, \\overline{BC} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />.\nOur answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a76ba4f890c1c119b3ae9ab082eb336d6556fd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 * 48 + 12 = \\boxed{108}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"149\" height=\"25\" />.\n- whatRthose\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2015_AIME_I_11.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/2015_AIME_I_11.png/270px-2015_AIME_I_11.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"270\" height=\"326\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/2015_AIME_I_11.png/405px-2015_AIME_I_11.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/f2/2015_AIME_I_11.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a02a2fe778a7992d8a056f094010202940d725c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, BM = x, AB = y, \\angle IBM = \\alpha.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35bb3f3bcadf5dc5c045b80fc24d014c0b969cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac84c6097f499cf1e5e0014495083169c90d50e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e043291550f1ccf707896978319b4c1b4364d127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABM.$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd2ac684e8f5b1246e6cc763e10973015ee9a7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI = \\frac {2 xy \\cos \\alpha}{x+y} = 8, \\cos \\alpha = \\frac {x}{8} \\implies \\frac {x^2 y}{x+y} = 32.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"388\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd5a9ca09ecfa3a1879bf1d5bcdf28fa9c3422c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\frac {32 x} {x^2 - 32}.\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/3/db33a467b2c86363c2f40968ce9fea83e4dfd059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> is integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b76a451978e81698a69b97824e21ba562bdbb68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5.5^2 &lt; 32 \\implies x \\ge 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/78355f28ab1aeee78d0eb5f845e4345cc4141b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM &lt; BI \\implies x =\\{ 6, 6.5, 7, 7.5 \\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"281\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195b36843a0e06fc82bd91e52ea401b078aadb01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not integer. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0ac050de367b7cd32d924f23281dd135e0136d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 6 \\implies y = 48 \\implies 2(x+y) =  \\boxed{\\textbf{108}}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"22\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/R8kvayz7Rtw?si=hFg4yGZO4dxyxAuG\">https://youtu.be/R8kvayz7Rtw?si=hFg4yGZO4dxyxAuG</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I\" title=\"2015 AIME I\">2015 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Proble